{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "COL",
  "chapter": 4,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "COL.4.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:COL.4.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Masters, give to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "your",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " servants that which is just and equal; knowing that ye also have a Master in heaven.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "COL.4.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:COL.4.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Continue in prayer, and watch in the same with thanksgiving;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "COL.4.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:COL.4.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "At the same time praying also for us, that God would open to us a door of utterance, to speak the mystery of Christ, for which I am also in bonds:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "COL.4.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:COL.4.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That I may make it manifest, as I ought to speak.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "COL.4.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:COL.4.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Walk in wisdom towards them that are without, redeeming the time.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "COL.4.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:COL.4.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let your speech ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " always with grace, seasoned with salt, that ye may know how ye ought to answer every man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "COL.4.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:COL.4.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All my state shall Tychicus declare to you, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a beloved brother, and a faithful minister and fellow-servant in the Lord:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "COL.4.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:COL.4.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whom I have sent to you for the same purpose, that he may know your state, and comfort your hearts;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "COL.4.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:COL.4.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With Onesimus, a faithful and beloved brother, who is ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of you. They will make known to you all things which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are done",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " here.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "COL.4.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:COL.4.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Aristarchus, my fellow-prisoner, saluteth you; and Marcus, sister's son to Barnabas, (concerning whom ye received commandments: if he should come to you, receive him;)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "COL.4.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:COL.4.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jesus, who is called Justus, who are of the circumcision. These only ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fellow-workers to the kingdom of God, who have been a comfort to me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "COL.4.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:COL.4.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Epaphras, who is ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of you, a servant of Christ, saluteth you, always laboring fervently for you in prayers, that ye may stand perfect and complete in all the will of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "COL.4.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:COL.4.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I bear him testimony, that he hath a great zeal for you, and them ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in Laodicea, and them in Hierapolis.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "COL.4.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:COL.4.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Luke, the beloved physician, and Demas, greet you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "COL.4.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:COL.4.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Salute the brethren who are in Laodicea, and Nymphas, and the church which is in his house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "COL.4.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:COL.4.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when this epistle is read among you, cause that it be read also in the church of the Laodiceans; and that ye likewise read the ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "epistle",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from Laodicea.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "COL.4.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:COL.4.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And say to Archippus, take heed to the ministry which thou hast received in the Lord, that thou fulfill it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "COL.4.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:COL.4.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The salutation by the hand of me Paul. Remember my bonds. Grace ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with you. Amen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
